SUMMARY:Middle Grey Arts & Heritage - Shoreline Chorus - Gilbert & Sullivan's 'The Pirates of Penzance'
DESCRIPTION:The wonderful singers and musicians of the Shoreline Chorus are back at Annesley\, Markdale with a concert version of The Pirates of Penzance\, a tale of Victorian piracy and love\, both delightful and complicated from the repertoire of Gilbert & Sullivan. \n​Shoreline is a 50 member soprano-alto-tenor-bass (SATB) Owen Sound based community choir under the direction of Ann-Marie MacDairmid. Ann-Marie started Shoreline simply out of a desire\, “… to conduct her own choir and sing music that I wish I had had an opportunity to sing when I was to high school.” They have developed very far down that road\, touring and providing audiences around the region with passionate\, funny\, and dramatic performances. \nTickets $35 \nFamily Special $60 \nOnline\, at Annesley\, or at-the-door \n​Doors open at 6:30 pm \nShow starts at 7:00 pm
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/middle-grey-arts-heritage-shoreline-chorus-gilbert-sullivans-the-pirates-of-penzance/
LOCATION:Annesley United Church\, 82 Toronto St S\, Markdale\, Ontario\, N0C 1H0\, Canada
GEO:44.3172054;-80.6460147
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Annesley United Church 82 Toronto St S Markdale Ontario N0C 1H0 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=82 Toronto St S:geo:-80.6460147,44.3172054
END:VEVENT
