SUMMARY:Emancipation Festival Speaker’s Corner
DESCRIPTION:The Emancipation Festival\, in partnership with Grey Roots Museum & Archives\, invites you to an evening of engaging dialogue with educators\, historians and descendants of freedom seekers. Celebrate 164 years of the longest continuous festival in North America! \n● Bobby Dean Blackburn (music during reception)\n● Legacy – From the Past\, Present and Future speakers and a performance from the Mellish Dancers\n● Guest speakers: Dorothy Abbott\, Lesa Walker and Carolynn and Sylvia Wilson \nAdmission fee is $25. Purchase tickets in advance or at the door. \nAppetizers will be provided and refreshments will be available. Doors open at 6 p.m.\, and the program starts at 7 p.m. Space is limited so don’t delay\, get your ticket today! \n 
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/emancipation-festival-speakers-corner/
LOCATION:Grey Roots Museum & Archives\, 102599 Grey Road 18\, RR4\, Owen Sound\, Ontario\, N4K 5N6\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Emancipation Festival":MAILTO:owensoundemancipationfestival@gmail.com
GEO:44.5211579;-80.9414635
